<title>UK: EMU could have serious consequences - UK's Blair.</title>
<headline>EMU could have serious consequences - UK's Blair.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The creation of a single currency in the European Union could have &quot;very, very serious consequences&quot; if it was mishandled, opposition Labour leader Tony Blair said on Sunday.</p>
<p>Speaking in a BBC television interview, Blair declined to rule out Britain joining a single currency in 1999 under a Labour government, but repeated his pledge to call a referendum on the issue if it was proposed to ditch sterling.</p>
<p>But he added: &quot;If it is not done properly, it could have very, very serious consequences.&quot; -- London Newsroom +44 171 5427950</p>
